  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Clearing is expected behind a cold front tonight, \nfollowed by seasonable temperatures through this weekend.\n\nDeep moisture and a cold front have moved east of the region this \nafternoon. A secondary cold front/surface trough will move across \nthe region, bringing a low chance of showers across north-central NY \nthrough this evening. Surface high pressure will build into the \nregion tonight. Cooler weather is expected with low temperatures \nfalling into the 40s, and the upper 30s across the interior Southern \nTier and portions of the North Country. Patchy fog is expected \nacross valley locations especially across the western Southern Tier \nand Black River Valley late tonight. \n\nHigh pressure will move across the region this weekend, reaching New \nEngland by Sunday. A southerly flow will increase Sunday and warmer \nair will move into the region. Highs will range from the low to mid \n60s Saturday to the mid to upper 60s Sunday. A progressive shortwave \ntrough and jet streak is expected to move across the region Sunday. \nIncreasing warmth and moisture and large scale lift may result in \nscattered showers across north-central NY Sunday afternoon. \n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Below average temperatures with frost potential \nearly next week.\n\nA deep 500mb trough will move across eastern Canada and the \nNortheast early next week. A strong cold front will cross the \nforecast area late Sunday night. While a few showers are possible \nalong the cold front, the primary focus will be the cooler weather \nfor the eastern Great Lakes region Monday through Tuesday night. \n850mb temperatures are expected to fall to 0C to -2C. This will \nsupport daytime highs in the 50s, and the upper 40s across the \nhigher terrain. Low temperatures are expected to fall into the 30s \nand frost is possible inland from the Lakes Monday night and Tuesday \nnight.",
